entries.summary:
Mortar's Vite plugin. Add it next to `@solidjs/vite-plugin`:

```ts
import { mortarKit } from '@mortar-kit/admin/vite';
import midnight from '@mortar-kit/theme-midnight';

export default defineConfig({ plugins: [solid({ ... }), mortarKit({ theme: midnight })] });
```

examples:
```ts
export const members = defineCollection({
  name: 'members',
  label: 'Members',
  fields: { email: fields.text({ label: 'Email', required: true }), name: fields.text({ label: 'Name' }) },
});
createAuth({ methods, secret, authorize: allowMembers({ content, collection: 'members' }) });
```

```ts
// src/server/auth.ts
export const auth = authFromEnv({ store: createJsonFileStore({ dir: '.data' }), siteName: 'My site' });
```

```ts
const auth = createAuth({
  methods: [google({ clientId, clientSecret }), email({ mailer, store })],
  authorize: allowEmails(['you@example.com', '*@example.com']),
  secret: process.env.MORTAR_AUTH_SECRET!,
});
```

```ts
// src/middleware.ts (vite.config: solid({ start: { middleware: './src/middleware.ts' } }))
export default createMiddleware({ auth, blobs });
```

members.doc:
Keeps pending sign-ins (hashes, for minutes). Any ContentStore works;
with the JSON-file store, use a directory outside your content and git
(e.g. `createJsonFileStore({ dir: '.data' })`).

examples:
```ts
email({ mailer: resendMailer({ apiKey: process.env.RESEND_API_KEY!, from: 'Site <admin@example.com>' }), store });
```

entries.summary:
Where documents live: raw data by collection name and slug. Implement it
to keep content anywhere (files, a database, an API). Deliberately dumb;
`createContent` applies every rule.

examples:
```ts
export const posts = defineCollection({
  name: 'posts',
  label: 'Posts',
  fields: { title: fields.text({ label: 'Title', required: true }), date: fields.date({ label: 'Date' }) },
  body: true,
  sort: { field: 'date', order: 'desc' },
});
```

```ts
// src/entry-client.tsx
if (hasIslands()) {
  const { bricks } = await import('./bricks/index.ts');
  hydrateIslands({ bricks, actions: islandActions({ action: brickActions.action, run: runBrickAction }) });
} else {
  const { Root } = await import('./Root.tsx');
  hydrate(() => <Root />, document);
}
```

